pp.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fnest%2FQxhwr-WmT4SJslNqZ41Mbb0DDmYwHE6JWScjj6N3Xy0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fnest%2FQxhwr-WmT4SJslNqZ41Mbb0DDmYwHE6JWScjj6N3Xy0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br><br>Based on the above information, the correct statement(s) is/are","options":["the separation of the compounds depends on their degree of adsorption","the compound Q moves faster than the compound P","the compound R moves slower than the compounds P and Q","the compound $S$ (see above figure) is expected to move slower than the compound R"],"answer":3,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NEST (NISER) 2018","_marksId":"68091fef3a10446a207fdc71"},{"id":86104,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NEST (NISER)","q":"A mixture contains 4-methylaniline, 2-naphthol, 3-chlorobenzoic acid and 1,3-dinitrobenzene. The following scheme of separation is used to separate its constituents.<br><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fnest%252FarFzluXp2jGF6k_ll3i3avJO7F9BZ0cubdEofce8SQE.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fnest%2FarFzluXp2jGF6k_ll3i3avJO7F9BZ0cubdEofce8SQE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fnest%2FarFzluXp2jGF6k_ll3i3avJO7F9BZ0cubdEofce8SQE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br><br>The correct statement(s) regarding the separation method is/are:","options":["The reagents in Step 2 and Step 3 can be interchanged (i.e. aq. NaOH in Step 2 and aq. $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$ in Step 3).","Y is 3-chlorobenzoic acid.","W and Z are 4-methylaniline and 1,3-dinitrobenzene respectively.","If the original mixture also contains 4 -aminobenzoic acid, it will be present in the filtrate of Step 1."],"answer":3,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NEST (NISER) 2017","_marksId":"68091fed3a10446a207fdc63"},{"id":86105,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NEST (NISER)","q":"The compound that produces aromatic species upon deprotonation of the indicated hydrogen is:","options":["<img style=\"width: 130px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-ea2a394b356f0fa5.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-ea2a394b356f0fa5.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-ea2a394b356f0fa5.png\">\n<img style=\"width: 130px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fiat_nest%2Fpyq_2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fnest_2026__q22_d4.png?alt=media\" />","<img style=\"width: 80px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-29fa0d9faee944c4.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-29fa0d9faee944c4.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-29fa0d9faee944c4.png\">\n<img style=\"width: 80px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fiat_nest%2Fpyq_2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fnest_2026__q22_d1.png?alt=media\" />","<img style=\"width: 50px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-7a7fcd5b900b1ff1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-7a7fcd5b900b1ff1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-7a7fcd5b900b1ff1.png\">\n<img style=\"width: 50px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fiat_nest%2Fpyq_2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fnest_2026__q22_d2.png?alt=media\" />","<img style=\"width: 100px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-b003a737e07007f4.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-b003a737e07007f4.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-b003a737e07007f4.png\">\n<img style=\"width: 100px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fiat_nest%2Fpyq_2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fnest_2026__q22_d3.png?alt=media\" />"],"answer":1,"solution":"For a species to be aromatic, it must be cyclic, planar, completely conjugated, and contain $(4n+2)\\pi$ electrons (Huckel's rule).<br><br>Deprotonation involves the removal of $H^{+}$ to form a carbanion.<br><br>In compound (1), deprotonation forms a carbanion that can delocalize to form an enolate, but the ring contains an $sp^{3}$ hybridized carbon, so it lacks complete conjugation. It is non-aromatic.<br><br>In compound (2), deprotonation yields the 5-methylcyclopentadienyl anion. The ring is cyclic, planar, completely conjugated, and possesses $6\\pi$ electrons ($4$ from two double bonds and $2$ from the carbanion lone pair). This satisfies the $(4n+2)\\pi$ rule for $n=1$, making the species aromatic.<br><br>In compound (3), deprotonation gives the 3-methylcyclopropenyl anion. The ring is fully conjugated but has $4\\pi$ electrons. It satisfies the $4n\\pi$ rule for $n=1$, making it antiaromatic.<br><br>In compound (4), deprotonation forms the 7-methylcycloheptatrienyl anion. The conjugated ring has $8\\pi$ electrons. It satisfies the $4n\\pi$ rule for $n=2$, making it antiaromatic.<br><br>Therefore, compound (2) produces an aromatic species upon deprotonation.<br><br>Answer : <img style=\"width: 80px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fiat_nest%2Fpyq_2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fnest_2026__q22_d1.png?alt=media\" />","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NEST (NISER) 2026","_marksId":"6a45fe505aa758e832e06ea5","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect"},{"id":86106,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NEST (NISER)","q":"The compounds represented by the following two structures are<br><br><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fnest%252FU78OnnvGV8QvUJXIvwatqGk2_THAzBP2H9QxyOyXYHM.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fnest%2FU78OnnvGV8QvUJXIvwatqGk2_THAzBP2H9QxyOyXYHM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fnest%2FU78OnnvGV8QvUJXIvwatqGk2_THAzBP2H9QxyOyXYHM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["Enantiomers.","not related to each other.","identical.","Anomers."],"answer":0,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NEST (NISER) 2021 (Session 2)","_marksId":"68091ff83a10446a207fdcd0"},{"id":86107,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NEST (NISER)","q":"The IUPAC name of the compound $\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{COOCH}_3$ is","options":["pent-3-en-2-one","butenyl ethanoate","methyl butanoate"